EXT. MONUMENT VALLEY

\*tap\* \*tap\* \*crack\* \*sizzle\*

Extreme Closeup of an egg sizzling in a cast iron skillet

We cut wider to reveal a young girl, Alexis, wearing cowboy attire, cooking her breakfast on an open fire, sipping coffee from a tin cup. A black and white cat with different colored eyes, Mags, sits on her lap, napping.

Alexis is relaxed and slides the fried egg from the pan to a tin plate but before she can dig in, she pauses, her eyes narrow. She puts her index finger in her mouth to wet it and holds it up to test the wind.

ALEXIS
Well, Mags, looks like we’re going to have to cut breakfast short…

She forks the egg into her mouth and downs it in one gulp.

ALEXIS
…storm‘s comin‘ faster than we anticipated. We gotta get the herd moving if we wanna make it to the ranch before it catches us.

A wider view reveals a nasty storm brewing in the distance, with roiling clouds and thunder echoing across the plain.

Alexis mounts her horse, Mags is securely on her shoulder. She drives the horse forward and steers it expertly, getting the cattle moving. It’s looking good at first but as we pan around the storm is closing in, the cattle start to panic.

Alexis steels herself, she’s unflappable. She pushes her steed to increase the pace. The thunder in the distance isn’t as loud as the thunder of the herd running around her.

The storm is on top of them now, wind whipping hard. Alexis’ hat blows off and up into the sky, gone.

We see the intense focus on her face. She’s determined to make it.

We pull back slightly to reveal Mags is no longer on her shoulder but instead a cat-sized horse. She turns her head and their eyes lock, both are startled.

Alexis looks down and she’s riding a horse-sized Mags! Nothing makes sense! Mags slowly turns her head towards Alexis without breaking stride…

MAGS
Alexis, time to get up. Do you hear me? You’re going to be late.

INT. ALEXIS' BEDROOM

The image of Alexis riding a giant horse-sized version of Mags is suddenly replaced with Alexis wrestling a big pillow.

Alexis is wide-eyed and a little crazed looking as the reality of the waking world sets in. Her mother is casually standing at the door to Alexis’ room, unsurprised to see her daughter in such disarray.

MARTINA
Breakfast in 5, can you do it?

ALEXIS
Yes, ma’am. Right away ma’am.

Alexis gives her mom an over-the-top salute then rigidly falls over and on to the floor from her bed. Her mother, Martina, rolls her eyes and walks away to the kitchen.

INT. SANTIAGO KITCHEN

Alexis, walks into the kitchen, fully dressed but struggling to get her hair into place, one chunk of her hair is refusing to give up the bed head look.

Alexis looks at the table and looks visibly tense. Her father, Eric, looks up from his cereal, sees his daughter tensing up, a sense of urgency coming to his face. He looks at the table and immediately straightens the cereal box, milk carton and fork so everything is at 90 degree angles. Alexis relaxes.

ALEXIS
Thanks Dad.

ERIC
No problem kiddo.

Breakfast continues uneventfully, but Alexis starts to eye the door, the dread of school is approaching.

MARTINA
Can I…?

Martina gestures towards Alexis’ hair.

ALEXIS
Yes please, it won’t stay down.

Martina wets her fingers in the kitchen sink and manages to tame the rebel chunk of hair.

INT. SANTIAGO FOYER

Alexis grabs her large backpack, put's her big headphones on around her neck.

ALEXIS
Laters! Love ya!

ERIC
Love you too kiddo!

MARTINA
Have a good day!

Alexis pats the large Elvis Presley statue standing by the door on the head, for good luck. It's well-worn in that spot, seemingly a household tradition. We briefly see there is actually a fair amount of Elvis memorabilia in the living room, a mini-shrine of sorts.

EXT. SANTIAGO FRONT YARD

Alexis begins the walk to school, the look of dread now very apparent on her face. She pulls on her big headphones, eyes straight ahead, marching onward toward destiny. We hear an indie pop song with a good beat to walk to.

EXT. SUBURBAN NEIGHBORHOOD

Alexis walks away from her turn-of-the-century Craftsman-style house, and we see the rest of the neighborhood which is just an endless parade of cookie-cutter boring ranch houses with identical lawns.

Alexis is focused on getting to school unscathed. She's dodging skateboarders, lemonade stands, gigantic SUV's with distracted parents driving their kids to school.

One such SUV wipes the screen and now we see a World War 1 warzone, Alexis in infantry gear with a large backpack. She's marching across field between the trenches, mortars going off on either side. An explosion wipes the frame again and we're back to reality.

EXT. MAIN STREET

She passes a couple shops on the town's Main Street. There's a fancy Starbucks-like coffee shop that's a tad ill-fitting amongst the more mom-and-pop shops.

A man is sitting nearby playing a bluesy song on a harmonica, he's got a kind and sympathetic face, and a raggedy cardboard sign asking for donations. Alexis smiles at him and drops a couple coins in his checked hat. He makes a grateful hand gesture without missing a beat and continues playing.

EXT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL

She's made it in one piece as she arrives at the entryway to the school. She tries to not draw attention as she passes the final gauntlet, the "cool" kids hanging on a nearby bench. In slow motion we see her make the fatal mistake, eye contact. The "cool" kid's eyes narrow with predatory smiles creeping across their faces. A quick flash in Alexis' mind sees hyenas grouped together and eyeing their lunch, her. She pushes open the door and rushes in but knows the worst is yet to come.

INT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL HALLWAY

Alexis heads to her locker, a teacher points to her headphones, indicating she needs to take them off. She puts the large headphones in her locker, hanging on a hook. Where other kids might have photos of their friends or a summer vacation on the inside of the door, Alexis has photos of her favorite stuffed animals and her cat Mags. She grabs her history book and associated notebook and heads to class.

INT. HISTORY CLASS

Alexis sits down, heart sinking as she's already hearing snickering from the "cool" kids we met at the entryway. She attempts to bridge the gap...

ALEXIS
Hey guys (nervously).

...only to be met with silence and glaring. She averts her eyes and waits for class to start.

We see the clock on the wall move forward.

MR.HENCHER
So, I hope you all did the reading last night. Let’s see, uh, Chut.

Charles “Chut” Utmore, the leader of the “cool“ kids, a broad shouldered boy, square jawed, with immaculately coiffed blonde hair, smiled confidently. He was in love with the sound of his own voice and was about to show it.

MR.HENCHER
Chut, what was the 19th amendment about?

CHUT
Passed in 1920, the 19th Amendment allowed women the right to vote, marking what many consider to be the last major barrier for gender equality.

Chut turns to Cindy and smiles.

CHUT
(whispering) Nailed it!

Chut and Cindy fist bump.

Alexis' eye starts to twitch with that last sentence. She's sitting silently, but looks like she's going to explode.

ALEXIS
(speaking internally) Let it go. You don't need to address it. Just let it...

We see Alexis' eyes look down at her right hand, it's slowly starting to rise.

ALEXIS
(continues internally) What are you doing? Hand, do not move any further!

Her hand continues to move upward, it's clearly moving with a lot of resistance but it's not about to stop.

MR.HENCHER
Thanks Chut. Any questions?

Alexis' hand shoots up like a rocket, hand waving impatiently.

ALEXIS
(cont. internally) No. Stop. Don't. Say. Anything.

MR.HENCHER
(reluctantly) Yes, Alexis?

ALEXIS
Um, sorry, but I think there's more to it than that. While the 19th Amendment was a crucial step forward, it wasn't the end of the struggle for women's equality. Women, especially women of color, still face numerous barriers. They continue to face voter suppression tactics, discrimination in the workplace, and unequal access to education. Even today, the gender pay gap and underrepresentation in leadership roles persist. So, I don't think we can say the 19th Amendment was the last barrier for women's equality.

Mr.Hencher is about to respond, nervously, when the bell rings and the kids all get up and run for the door.

A girl with pink hair and a soccer jersey with the number 15 on it, passes Alexis.

MEGAN
(softly) Smash the patriarchy.

Alexis shows a rare smile, but it's short-lived as lunch is next.

INT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL CAFETERIA

Alexis is standing in the lunch line when her turn comes up.

JORGE
What'll it be today, wait, wait, I know it!

ALEXIS
(smiling) PB and J and a milk please.

JORGE
Ah I had it, you've got to give me a chance to guess though!

ALEXIS
Next time, Jorge.

JORGE
Maybe you want to try my fantastic curry instead?

ALEXIS
No thanks, I'm a creature of habit.

JORGE
All good, buen provecho!

ALEXIS
Gracias!

That was the pleasant part of lunch, Alexis smile fades as she turns towards the cafeteria tables. Most of the faces are indifferent, others imply "don't sit here". Some even go as far as to block a space.

As she passes by Chut and his crew's table, Chut "accidentally" puts his foot out and Alexis trips. Her tray flies up and in her attempt to catch it, her backpack comes off and a well-loved stuffed rabbit comes out.

Chut's expression changes from feigned surprise at tripping Alexis to a maliciously happy one. He bends over and pretends to help Alexis but goes right for the rabbit.

CHUT
(in a mocking tone) Is this your friend? How cute.

ALEXIS
(flustured, furious) Give him back Chut.

CHUT
Of course, of course, I wouldn't want something to happen to him, I can be so clumsy.

Alexis' heart is sinking, she doesn't know what's coming but it won't be good and Dr.Hopps is not in good hands.

Chut cradles the stuffed rabbit in his hands, overdoing the gesture as he hands it back to Alexis. Right before it's in her grasp he "trips" throwing it upward.

In slow motion we see the horror in Alexis' eyes, she makes a strong effort to grab the stuffed rabbits leg as it moves upward, but misses and it sails over her.

All eyes are on her and the flying rabbit. It's tumbling towards some unsuspecting kids eating their lunch.

Chut's eyes narrow as he watches with evil delight as the white rabbit is landing dead-center in a full bowl of yellow curry. It splashes all the nearby students and as time returns to normal speed, curry splashes Alexis in the face as well.

CHUT
(stifling laughter) Oh no! I am so sorry!

Chut's nasty crew is giggling as well. Alexis wipes the curry from her face, grabs the rabbit and her backpack and runs out of the cafeteria.

EXT. SUBURBAN NEIGHBORHOOD

Alexis runs home, almost holding her breathe, about to explode. She runs up to her house and crashes through the front door.

INT. SANTIAGO FOYER

Alexis, a tornado of jacket, shoes, papers, books, headphones, sheds her stuff in the entryway and flies up the stairs.

A door opens and her father, who was sitting at a computer in the home office, nervously peaks out to see what the noise was and eyes the items strewn about.

INT. ALEXIS' BEDROOM

Alexis dives into her stuffed animal pile headfirst, sobbing.

ALEXIS
(crying) I just want a friend. A single solitary friend...

MAGS
(softly) mew?

Alexis stops sobbing so hard, peaking her head out from behind a big stuffed Crocodile to see Mags. She can’t help but smile a little through the sobs.

ALEXIS
(sob laughing) Of course, you’re the best friend anyone could ever have, but you know, it would be nice to have a human friend too.

MAGS
Meow mew mrrrrow

ALEXIS
I know, people suck. But still, I am people, it would just, you know, be nice.

Outside her door her father, who had just come up to check hears this and is visibly heartbroken for his daughter. He briefly looks like he’s going to quietly go back downstairs, but then turns and bursts through the door.

ERIC
Alexis Santiago, you’re the best. You’re amazing and brilliant and funny and clever and anyone that doesn’t see it is just… just… a damn fool!

Alexis, now laughing through her tears, holding Mags and seeing her dad standing so intensely, arm out and dramatically pointing upward with his index finger to emphasize his point. He softens a bit as her laughter continues, he’s laughing too and she gives him a hug.

Alexis goes to her backpack and takes out Dr.Hopps and holds him up for her father to see. It's half covered in curry.

ERIC
Hmmm. Dr.Hopps may never be the same but let's see what we can do.

INT. ALEXIS' BEDROOM - NIGHT

Alexis is finishing up her homework at her desk, room illuminated only be her desk lamp. A stained Dr.Hopps can be seen on her desk. She stretches, sighs, and then slumps down with a comically grouchy look on her face.

ALEXIS
It’s only Tuesday. Something’s got to give but it’s not going to be me!

Alexis stand like her father did earlier, pointing upward for emphasis then dramatically walks over to her bed, littered with stuffed animals, Mags sleeping amongst them. She falls into bed like a tree falling, flinging Mags and various stuffed animals into the air. Mags is mildly irritated but cuddles up anyway and they fall asleep.

The clock on the bedside table say’s 11:59, then the analog numbers flip to 12:00, midnight.

There’s suddenly a light being cast on Alexi’s sleeping face. It’s coming from the closet so it’s casting a lined pattern through the slats in the closet door. Alexis stirs, sensing this eerie light on her face.

It feels like a dream. Alexis stands up groggily, wearing her baggy pajamas. Mags is also curious and follows after.

ALEXIS
Huh? What is that?

Cautiously. Alexis opens the closet door, pushes aside some junk to reveal the back wall of her closet, the light is coming from behind the wallpaper.

ALEXIS
What the…?

She finds an edge and tears it away, revealing a small square door in the wall, ornately decorated and about half of a meter tall and wide. There is a bright pulsing light coming from behind it, leaking around the edges.

ALEXIS
Looks like… and old laundry hatch or something, I never knew it was here. What’s this light?

Mags creeps near as well, both fascinated by this strange door in her closet. Alexis opens it slowly at first but now that the seal is broken, the door blasts open and sucks them in, instantly.

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

Alexis and Mags are screaming through a cosmic tunnel towards an identical door as in her closet, they hit it full force, blasting through and rolling as they hit the ground on the other side of the door.

Alexis collects herself and checks on Mags.

ALEXIS
What on earth was that?! You ok kitty?

MAGS
mrrow

ALEXIS
Where are we?

Alexis looks up and around and is stunned. It’s an enormous room, a bizarre atrium of an Escher-esque hotel containing an extremely broad range of architectural styles. Ancient looking stone doors, victorian, brutalist, futuristic, every kind of door one can imagine, embedded into the walls at confusing angles, defying logic.

We pull out very wide and Alexis and Mags are tiny dots on the screen, dwarfed by hundreds of doors and hallways. A giant intricate barometer-looking chandelier floats in the center, it‘s generating a low hum and rotating slowly on changing axis.

ALEXIS
I don‘t think this is my closet, Mags.

MAGS
(softly) mew

ALEXIS
Hello?

No answer but a spooky echo of her own voice. Alexis walks to a nearby door and carefully turns the handle and peaks through.

ALEXIS
Anyone here? Hello?

As she opened the door we can see another door in the deep and way up opening at the same time. Alexis looks down to see herself and Mags 20 meters below, peaking through a door. She panics, pulls back and slams the door shut.

ALEXIS
Jiminy Christmas! What IS this PLACE?!
She gathers her courage, opens the door and peaks again. It’s definitely weird but it somehow seems fine. She closes the door and tries another. This one seems to lead to a stairway, she ventures through, keeping the door open, She sees Mags, standing on the ceiling way above her, or is she on the ceiling above Mags?

Physics in this world seem to follow different rules. After the initial shock this is actually pretty interesting. Mags sees a cat-sized door and runs through it. She’s now in a totally different part of this atrium.

MAGS
Mrrow?

ALEXIS
(laughing) I think it’s actually fine Mags, let me see if I can come to you.
Alexis walks ahead and enters another door, at a strange angle. She comes out a little closer but too far to reach Mags and with gravity seemingly working at a 45 degree difference. She proceeds to try more doors, it’s actually pretty fun. She sees a small gap between one ledge and another that is 90 degrees different than the one she’s standing on, she holds her breath and jumps, gravity adjusts with her!

This is actually really fun. She’s now running through doors, jumping from ledges, even Mags has the hang of it now and they are slowly working their way to one another. They are now on the same path and Alexis is running towards the door, laughing, with Mags right behind her. She notices just a bit too late that this door looks a bit different, it’s old and poorly nailed together, it looks like it might fall apart! She blasts through it, but this time it doesn’t open to another spot in the atrium.

EXT. PICKENS, MISSISSIPPI - HIGHWAY 51 - EARLY MORNING - 1956

Alexis and Mags roll out of the doorway of the skeleton of an old shack, into the grass on the side of a highway. She sit’s up, checking herself for injuries but is luckily fine. As she stands up, brushing the dirt off herself, she notices the door she came through, slowly closing, then completely falling off the doorframe that it was barely attached to to begin with. She and Mags watch in horror as it falls in slow motion and breaks into pieces, beyond repair.

ALEXIS
(panicked) This is fine. Totally fine. Fine. Fine. Fine. Fine… Just breathe. Breathe.

Alexis looks at Mags, Mags looks up, worried.

ALEXIS
I know, it's not fine. Not fine at all. Where are we now? It's so hot and humid.

It's early morning, next to Highway 51 near Pickens, Mississippi. The surrounding area is deserted, the road is empty, it would nice if it wasn't so eerie.

ALEXIS
Ok, if we follow this road, it's bound to lead to some sort of civilization. It's not like we've been banished to some bizarro liminal space between realities right?

MAGS
Mrrow?

ALEXIS
(nervously) Right, right, that would be ridiculous, what am I thinking he he he. Oh man...

They walk down the road, the drone of late summer Cicadas can be heard clearly, punctuating the eerie quality of the environment.

Soon they come across a billboard saying "Pickens Motel - 10 Miles ahead on Highway 51. Free Parking - Swimming Pool - Air Conditioning. Pet-Friendly"

ALEXIS
10 Miles??!?!

EXT. PICKENS MOTEL - 1956

Alexis and Mags, slowly, finally, arrive at the entrance to the Pickens Motel, it looks brand new and quite nice, but very vintage looking.

ALEXIS
(panting from the heat) Whoa, pretty retro, not too shabby.

MAGS
(impressed) Meyow.

INT. PICKENS MOTEL LOBBY - 1956

Alexis walks in to the main building, a bell rings as the door opens and closes, alerting the desk attendant.

STANLEY
Hello young lady, how can I help you today?

Stanley, is the epitamy of 1950's style. Short ahir styled with pommade, browline glasses, white short-sleeved button down shirt and a skinny black tie.

ALEXIS
Wow, you guys are really committed to this vintage look.

STANLEY
Vintage? Are your parents around?

ALEXIS
That's actually why I'm here, I'm trying to call them, but I don't have my cell phone on me...

STANLEY
A what now? Um... you can use the phone as long as it's a local call.

ALEXIS
Well...that depends where we are...

STANLEY
(getting more and more confused) We're in Pickens.

ALEXIS
ok, Pickens... drawing a blank here.

STANLEY
Pickens, Mississippi.

Alexis is dumbfounded. This is quite far from home.

STANLEY
(nervously) Um...I think I need to check with my manager, I'll be back in a jiffy.

Stanley quickly goes into a back room and get's on the phone, nervously explaining the weird girl in her pajamas standing in the motel lounge.

Alexis taps her fingers on the desk, humming and waiting then starts to look around. There's a black and white television near some chairs it's playing a commercial for the Ed Sullivan show. A man is smoking a cigar and reading a newspaper, her eyes dart to the headline, "U.S. and Soviet Tensions Escalate Amidst Cold War Standoff". She waves away some smoke coughing, the smoking man in the brown suit gives her a weird look. She continues looking around, the clues are screaming at her every which way, it's the 1950's!

Opposite the smoking man is a man who looks amazingly like Elvis Presley. He’s occupied tracing a route north on a paper travel map.

As reality sinks in, she notices something out of the corner of her eye. A janitor closet door outside of the hotel lobby has a familiar glow around it, similar to the glow around the door in her closet.

Alexis looks at the attendant on the phone, makes a split-second decision, grabs Mags, interupting her cleaning ritual and runs out the door. The door bell rings and the attendant turns to see Alexis exit hastily.

EXT. PICKENS MOTEL - 1956

We’re standing on the far side of the parking lot seeing Alexis leave the hotel lobby. A figure in the foreground, sees her dramatic exit, sees her run to a strange glowing door, go through it. He sees the hotel attendant follow her, go to the same door and opens it revealing a cluttered and small cleaning closet with no sign of Alexis. The attendant is incredulous and confused.

We flip around to see the figure is a thin teenager with a shock of white hair and his small dog.

E
Woof!

SIX
Interesting indeed. Interesting indeed.

Six is casually propping big nails under each tire of a blue Cadillac Fleetwood with the license plate “GRCLAND“ visible.

SIX
C‘mon E, let‘s skedaddle.

Six picks up a leather messenger bag and with E in toe, walks over to the same door Alexis went through, but this time the glow is reddish. He enters and closes the door behind him. The attendant who was just about to return to the lobby, sees Six enter, runs back to the door a second time, throwing it open only to have a mop and bucket fall on him.

STANLEY
Aaaargh! What’s going on here!?

A young Elvis Presley, walks out of the hotel lobby. Get’s in his car to drive away and as he hits the gas all 4 tires pop and go flat.

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

Alexis and Mags are back in the atrium and they spot the small distinct door that leads back to her room.

ALEXIS
There's our door!

They book it to the door, hesitate slightly before opening it, get sucked in...

INT. ALEXIS' BEDROOM - NIGHT

A closeup on the bedside table clock, we see the number flip over to 12:01 am. After all of that, nearly no time has passed.

We rack focus tosee the bedroom closet door blast open, with Alexis and Mags tumbling out and into a pile of stuffed animals, launching them everywhere.

ALEXIS
We made it! I'm exhausted...

Alexis falls onto her bed and sound a sleep in moments. Mags walks over and cuddles in.

INT. ALEXIS' BEDROOM - MORNING

ERIC
Wakey wakey eggs ‘n bakey.

We see a POV of Alexis' eyes opening groggily and she turns to see her father is in the bedroom doorway.

ALEXIS
(half asleep) I’m vegetarian dad.

ERIC
I know, I know but eggs ‘n soy bacon substitute doesn’t have the same flow if ya know what I mean.

Alexis stifles her smile in her pillow.

ALEXIS
So cringe dad. Such a dork.

ERIC
I never said I wasn’t, up an at‘em sleepy head.

MAGS
(groggily) mrrrow?

ERIC
Yeah, you too Mags.

Eric leaves Alexis so she can get ready. She rubs her eyes and stumbles over to close her bedroom door and sees herself in the full length mirror.

ALEXIS
I had the weirdest dream last night…

She sees her pajamas are filthy and her eyes go wide.

ALEXIS
What the…

INT. SANTIAGO KITCHEN

A slightly stunned Alexis, now dressed for school sits at the breakfast table. Internally questioning her sanity.

MARTINA
Everything okay honey? You look like you’ve seen a ghost.

ALEXIS
(nervously) hehe all good, just had a weird dream last night, actually dad you’d get a kick out of it, I ran into Elvis in a hotel lobby.

Eric is reading news on his tablet at the table, he doesn’t look up from it.

ERIC
Elvis?

Alexis is surprised by the lack of reaction from her die-hard Elvis-fan-for-life father.

ALEXIS
(nervously) Presley?

ERIC
Sorry, I don’t follow, who?

Alexis is wide-eyed and really confused now.

ALEXIS
Nevermind. I’m off, don’t want to be late…

ERIC
Alright dear, see you after school.

INT. SANTIAGO FOYER

Alexis grabs her backpack and heads towards the door quickly to find what she feared, no Elvis statue, no mini-shrine to ”the King”, just a normal Foyer. Wordlessly, she opens the door and walks.

EXT. SANTIAGO FRONT YARD

Alexis pulls out her phone and starts searching her music service for Elvis Presley. No results. She almost falls over. A Hitchcock Vertigo camera effect shows us how she’s feeling, shocked and disoriented.

Then, she thinks. Flashes of the hotel lobby, the newspaper said September 8th, 1956. The framed photo in her dad’s shrine of Elvis‘ breakout performance on the Ed Sullivan show, what was that dated? September 9th! What happened? Did she somehow change time?

INT. SCIENCE CLASS

Alexis is sitting at her desk, focused on her own thoughts and more or less ignoring everything else.

ALEXIS
(Internally) If that wasn’t a dream, then I need to get back there, I need to find out what went wrong.

She’s anxiously checking the clock which is simply crawling. The second hand moving far too slow. She’s vaguely aware that Chut is eyeing her and about to say something nasty.

ALEXIS
Oh shut it Chut.

Chut is stunned by this preemptive denial and can say nothing.

Mercifully the bell rings, signifying the end of the school day. Alexis bolts out the door dramatically leaving everyone a little surprised.

EXT. MAIN STREET

Alexis is on a mission, she marches past the man playing harmonica, his eyes following her, wondering about the intensity of her walk. She leaves the frame, but a moment later her arm re-enters dropping a coin in his hat, he nods gratefully to her.

INT. SANTIAGO FOYER

Alexis blasts through the front door, but she’s not upset, she’s hyper-focused on her mission. Her father seems to have been waiting for her with a cup of hot cocoa.

ERIC
Hey kiddo! How was…

ALEXIS
Can’t talk, sorry, important homework.

Alexis rushes up the stairs.

ERIC
…school?

Eric just stands there for a beat then returns to his desk, sipping the hot cocoa intended for Alexis.

INT. ALEXIS' BEDROOM

Alexis enters the room quickly, Mags wakes up from her nap amongst the stuffed animals and stretches and walks over to Alexis.

ALEXIS
I’m not sure how Mags, but I think we changed something last night and I really think we need to fix it if we can.

Alexis opens her closet door, pushes aside the junk in her closet to reveal the back wall of her closet. There’s the door! She throws it open but it’s actually just an old laundry chute, it’s not glowing.

Alexis slumps over, dejected. Closing the door again.

ALEXIS
I don’t get it. Am I losing it Mags?

MAGS
Mrrow? Meow.

ALEXIS
I NEED to fix this Mags. I can’t be responsible for erasing Elvis‘ career!

Suddenly, the door starts glowing again. Alexis doesn’t see it until Mags starts scratching at the door. Alexis tentatively opens the door and they are sucked back into the bizarro atrium again!

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

Alexis is thrilled to be back, she wasn't crazy, this place wasn't a dream!

They walk forward to get a better view of the room. The door she went through last time to get to Pickens 1956 is gone, a brick wall in it's place.

ALEXIS
So how does this work? We can't just go through random doors, who knows where we might end up and if we'd be able to get back.

MAGS
(in agreement) meeow.

ALEXIS
How did we activate the door in my room? I said something right...

MAGS
meow

ALEXIS
I said I NEED to fix this and then it lit up. Well, I need to see what happened in 1956 that caused Elvis to somehow miss his big moment...

As she finishes the sentence, a draft blows through the room leading her to see a door in the distance start to glow, it looks like one of the room doors from the Pickens Motel!

ALEXIS
I think that's our door Mags, let's go!

EXT. PICKENS MOTEL - 1956

Alexis is standing at the door, it's softly pulsing with energy, she's excited and nervous but determined. She slowly pushes the door open, daylight floods through the door and she's looking at the parking lot. She sees herself, run into the janitors closet and disappear, then looking to the left, sees the blue cadillac and a mysterious teenager with white hair and his dog, walk into the same door but with a reddish glow. He disappears, Stanley opens the door and get clobbered with cleaning supplies.

ALEXIS
What on earth is going on? Who was that?

Alexis walks into the parking lot, leaving the door cracked open slightly. She sees Elvis walking to the car and is slightly star-struck, but quickly snaps out of it and heads towards him as he is entering the driver's seat.

ALEXIS
Wait!

ELVIS
Miss?

ALEXIS
Just... wait a second.

Alexis starts to inspect the car. A metallic glint underneath one of the tires catches her eye. She pulls up the nail, a satisfied smile crosses her face as she hold it up.

ELVIS
Wow, you've got some eagle eyes there young lady.

Alexis proceeds to find the remaining nails. Elvis is stunned and a bit confused.

ALEXIS
I think that's it.

ELVIS
Amazing, you just might have saved my career. I'm on my way to New York for an important gig, that would have stopped me for sure, what's your name?

ALEXIS
Alexis, and this is Mags

ELVIS
Well, Alexis and Mags, pleasure to meet you, thanks for the help!

Suddenly, Stanley notices Alexis from across the parking lot.

STANLEY
Hey! Come back here!

ALEXIS
(to Elvis) gotta go!

Elvis seeing the situation "convieniently" peels out, kicking up a cloud of dust, delaying Stanley from getting to Alexis before she's able to slip back through the door she arrived with.

Stanley, throws open the door, to find a surprised man in a bathing suit putting on suncreen. Once again, Stanley doesn't understand what's happening at all.

EXT. HOTEL NOWHERE

The Hotel Nowhere, a mish mash of architectural designs and structures spanning human civilization is floating in nothingness. Random objects and statues of greatly varying sizes are floating around us. We hear the signature sound of Alexis arriving through a door.

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

Alexis and Mags are on the floor, Alexis laughing and holding Mags.

ALEXIS
(giggling) Do you think that worked? Did we fix it?

The two head back to door to Alexis' room door.

INT. HOME OFFICE

Alexis, full of energy and anticipation swings open the door to find her father working on the computer.

ALEXIS
Who sings "Heartbreak Hotel"?

ERIC
Are you joking? The King himself, Elvis of course!

Alexis is relieved. It worked, she looks over and sees the shrine intact again as well.

ALEXIS
Thanks!

Alexis leaves the room as quickly as she arrived. Her father sits for a beat then turns back towards his work.

ERIC
(quietly to himself) ...but it wasn't "Heartbreak Hotel" it was "Heartbreak Motel", of course.

EXT. HOUSE OF EVERYWHERE

Reminiscent of the exterior view of the Hotel Nowhere, floating in a dark place in-between time and space we see a bizarre structure. It looks like someone jammed a hundred odd victorian mansions together at random angles. There are no windows but hundreds of doors, each unique in color and design. A creepy whooshing sound is all around us.

INT. HOUSE OF EVERYWHERE

Six and E come through a door, the janitor door they had used at the motel. They are standing in an impossibly long hallway filled with different kinds of doors.

They walk towards a particularly decrepit and eerie door with dark vines growing outward from the door frame, infecting and invading the surround doors and walls. It opens by itself with a creeking sound as they enter.

INT. THE VOID'S CHAMBER

The chamber is like an ancient attic and emanates tension. There is a large hole on the wall that is pure darkness, it is the source of the dark vines that grow along the walls towards the door. A subtle discordant hum creates an uneasy atmosphere. A voice is coming from the hole.

THE VOID
(in a hissing voice) You've failed.

Six is slightly caught off guard.

SIX
What do you mean?

THE VOID
It didn't work, you didn't disrupt the timeline at all, well, not in a way that really matters.

SIX
(Defensively) There...was another. A girl, a traveller like me.

THE VOID
Hmmph, no matter. Our work continues. We need to increase our efforts if I'm ever to be free of this prison.

SIX
And then you'll honor our deal?

THE VOID
Of course, dear child, of course.

EXT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL

It's a new day and Alexis is feeling positive, a bit less stuck. She had a wild experience and has a sense of accomplishment so there's a bit more pep in her step, perhaps this will be a good day?

She goes to push open the school's front door and smacks into the door face first, falling backwards, books and papers spilling out of her bag.

Chut and his gang are watching in amusement.

CHUT
You pull, genius. Like it says.

Alexis gathers her stuff, flustered. She looks up to see, it does in fact say "PULL" on the door.

ALEXIS
(to herself) The doors don't look new, they were always push before, right?

She pulls the door open, rubbing her face and feeling confused.

INT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL HALLWAY

Alexis arrives at her locker, enters the combination on her locker, pulls the handle but it doesn't open. She pauses, slightly surprised then tries again. No luck. She tries a final time then bangs her fist on the door in frustration. Chut is hovering nearby and smiles.

CHUT
So the trick is to turn the dial, then lift the handle. I know it's a bit advanced.

ALEXIS
(sarcastically) Thanks Chut. Big help.

CHUT
I'm here to help.

Chut walks away with his gang laughing, Alexis gives up and goes to class.

INT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL CAFETERIA

Alexis stands in line to buy lunch in the cafeteria. One of the workers puts food on the tray for the student in front of her.

JORGE
Next! Wait, wait, lemme guess, PB and J and a...

ALEXIS
(shyly smiling) and a milk please.

JORGE
(in friendly tone) and a milk. No chance at the meatloaf?

ALEXIS
It looks delicious but I'm a vegetarian.

JORGE
Ah right, sorry I forgot. I'll make a tofuloaf and win you over yet!

Alexis is smiling, but that fades fast as she sees Chut. Looks like it will be lunch in the library today.

INT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL LIBRARY

Alexis is sitting at a table alone, headphones on next to a stack of books. She unwraps the sandwich as she is looking at a book, casually takes a bite and stops. A look of horror comes across her face and she struggles to swallow. She opens the rest of the sandwich. It's some kind of green paste and strawberry jelly.

ALEXIS
(in disgust, to herself) Pickles. Why does this sandwich taste like pickles?!

A series of quick cut's show Alexis marching to the encyclopedias. She pulls out the "P" volume, blows off the dust. Slams it down on the table next to the offensive sandwich. Flips the pages expertly to "peanut", we follow her finger as it continues on, but instead of "peanut butter" we come to an entry titled "pickle butter" and there's an old black and white photograph of a man presenting pickle products, behind him, slightly out of focus and wearing a big fake mustache is a teenager with spiky white hair.

ALEXIS
I knew it!

Alexis slams the book shut, tosses the sandwich in a nearby trash can, and storms out of the library. The librarian, fruitlessly and far too late...

LIBRARIAN
Shhhhh!

INT. ALEXIS' BEDROOM

Alexis is packing a backpack with snacks, cat snacks, a flashlight, a notebook, a compass and other items from around her room. Mags is curiously overseeing the task.

ALEXIS
That kid, he was messing with Elvis which was bad enough, but peanut butter? Unthinkable!

MAGS
(in agreement) me-ow

ALEXIS
Door? Please open up so I can fix this!

On cue, the door comes to life. Alexis, confident in her purpose, moves through with no hesitation, Mags right behind her.

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

Alexis enters, on a mission. She takes a second to observe the floating barometer-like object in the center of the atrium. It seems to have a higher reading than before.

ALEXIS
Does that look different to you Mags?

Alexis shrugs and continues.

ALEXIS
I need to fix the peanut butter situation!

Alexis waits for a door to light up, but nothing.

ALEXIS
Hmm. Maybe that's not specific enough?

Alexis thinks a moment. For a moment we see into her impressive mind, flashes of pictures and text, a mind library of sorts. We see a book floating in darkness, it's got a big golden peanut on the cover. It's big and thick and represents her extensive knowledge on the topic of peanuts. The pages whir past and stop, a picture of George Washington Carver then the next page of him presenting the versatility of peanuts to the US Congress in 1921.

ALEXIS
I need to get to George Washington Carver in 1921!

The familiar breeze from before has returned! It's drawing Alexis' attention to a fancy wooden door that looks somehow congressional. She's about to open it but then pauses and looks at herself and her clothes.

ALEXIS
I think I'm going to stick out like a sore thumb in these clothes...

A hidden door opens on the nearby wall and within is a proper period outfit; a long dress with a high waistline and delicate embroidery, a wide brimmed hat, elbow length gloves. Alexis is thrilled but then looks closer at the boots which are high heeled and look supremely uncomfortable.

ALEXIS
uh-unh, no way.

EXT. WASHINGTON - CAPITOL BUILDING - 1921

Alexis and Mags step out on to the street. She's wearing the dress, hat and gloves, but she's kept her black and white Chuck Taylor Converse All-Stars and ditched the boots.

The view spins around to reveal the bustling streets and senators walking into the United States Capitol Building, along with members of the public also attending. Mags hops onto Alexis' shoulders and they fall in with the crowd.

INT. WASHINGTON - CAPTIOL BUILDING - 1921

As she enters the hearing room, she notices Six, wearing period clothing and a ridiculous fake moustache, working his way over to the senators.

George Washington Carver is sorting some papers and preparing to present his case for the agricultural importance of peanut farming. He's got a stack of charts to help his case.

MAGS
(urgently) meow!

ALEXIS
What is it?

Alexis follows the eye direction of Mags to see E is grabbing the charts in his mouth stealthily and pulling them away.

ALEXIS
(alarmed) What are they doing?

E starts pulling in a different stack of charts to replace the ones he took.

ALEXIS
Let's wait and see Mags, but keep a sharp eye on that dog.

The Senate committee chairman, Joseph W. Fordney, calls order and starts the proceedings.

FORDNEY
First up we have an agricultural presentation from Dr.Carver, let's begin.

Carver, put's up one of the charts that E replaced his own with, without looking at it and out of our view.

CARVER
Ladies and Gentlmen, today I would like to present to you the agricultural importance of... pickles?

Carver has turned to look at his chart and finally notices the replacement. It's a poorly made chart with the word "Pickles" in big letters and a primitive drawing of a pickle.

Posing as a senator himself, six speaks up as if speaking to his fellow senators.

SIX
(in a gravelly, pretend adult voice) Ah, yes, pickles! Excellent, excellent, I love pickles!

CARVER
I'm sorry my charts seem to be...

Six rapidly makes his way to the audience, putting on a hat to pretend to be another person.

SIX
(calling out from the audience) Yeah! Pickles are great! Pi-ckles, pi-ckles...

Six gestures that the audience should start chanting with him. They are confused but start to go along with him.

AUDIENCE
Pi-ckles, pi-ckles, pi-ckles.

FORDNEY
Order! Order!

CARVER
(to himself, deadpan) This is unexpected.

INT. GROCERY STORE - 2024

We see a view of a calm grocery store. An old man pushes a shopping cart very slowly. A bored employee is stocking peanut butter. Suddenly a time glitch flashes and the peanut butter turns to pickle butter. No one in the store notices.

INT. WASHINGTON - CAPTIOL BUILDING - 1921

Alexis takes action, this has to stop. Alexis and Mags run down to the presentation area and find E dragging away the peanut presentation.

ALEXIS
Stop that dog!

Mags, suddenly leaps into action, landing on the charts, startling E. E growls at Mags and Mags hisses back. That's enough conflict for E, who takes off.

Alexis grabs the charts...

INT. GROCERY STORE - 2024

A continuation of the view earlier and a new time glitch happens reverting the peanut products back to normal. Still, no one is aware anything is changing.

INT. WASHINGTON - CAPTIOL BUILDING - 1921

Alexis is on her way to George Washington Carver to return the proper charts amongst the chaos. The audience is split, some chanting "peanuts" some chanting "pickles", no one quite knowing why.

The police have been called and are coming in to calm the situation.

Six sees Alexis making her way to the presentation floor. He runs towards her.

SIX
You! What are you doing here?

ALEXIS
What are YOU doing here, you're messing with the timeline and with my life and with PEANUT BUTTER!

Six grabs the other side of the presentation charts and pulls them.

INT. GROCERY STORE - 2024

The peanuts revert to pickles again in a time glitch.

INT. WASHINGTON - CAPTIOL BUILDING - 1921

ALEXIS
Let go!

With one hand on the charts still she rips off Six' fake moustache.

SIX
Yowch!

Six lets go of the charts and soothes his face. Alexis takes the chance and manages to pass the charts back to George Washington Carver.

CARVER
Thank you. Arrest that saboteur!

Six realizes he's been found out, the police are making their way through the crowds towards him.

SIX
E! Time to go!

E is right by a door that has a reddish glow emanating from the other side. Six deftly scoops up E and jumps through the door.

INT. GROCERY STORE - 2024

The pickle butter reverts back to peanut butter. However, one jar of pickle butter remains. We see the the hand of an older man pick it up but his face is hidden from view but we can see his browline glasses.

STANLEY
Interesting...

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

Alexis and Mags enter the hotel, buzzing from their exciting victory, they wave back towards George Washington Carver through the closing door.

CARVER
Thanks again!

ALEXIS
Our pleasure! Good luck with your presentation!

The door closes and Alexis and Mags are alone in the hotel again.

Alexis and Mags look up and see that the barometer is in better shape although not notably better.

EXT. HOUSE OF EVERYWHERE

We fly silently through a small open door on the exterior and into the attic room containing the void, Six and E are entering...

INT. THE VOID'S CHAMBER

...they look defeated and are clearly nervous about talking to the Void. The room is buzzing with a dark energy.

THE VOID
(hissing) What happened? Did you fail again?

E
rrrrr

Six calms E who clearly doesn't like the tone of the Void.

SIX
It's this girl! Things were on track and she ruined it, her and her cat.

E
(growling at the memory of Mags) rrrrrrr

A beat passes, the energy in the room calms a bit.

THE VOID
(suddenly speaking in a sweeter tone) Six, my dear boy, I'm not upset with you, I merely want to remind you what's at stake here.

Six is looking down like a scolded child. E however is still looking at the Void intently, not trusting the tone change.

SIX
I know, I know. I'm trying!

THE VOID
I know you did, it's ok. It's just that I can't save your family in my current...condition. We need to tip the balance in order for me to help you.

SIX
I'm not sure what to do next.

THE VOID
Why I would think it would be obvious. We need to stop the girl. Stop her from interfering.

SIX
How is she traveling like me?

THE VOID
There is another...place...like this one. Kind of an inverted twin, she seems to be using it to sabotage our efforts.

SIX
How can I stop her?

THE VOID
I trust you'll do what's needed... in order to save your family of course.

Six and E leave the room, the mood is sullen and ominous. Six is deep in thought, figuring out the next move. E doesn't take his eyes off the Void as they leave.

The Void pulses menacingly at E, while Six is unaware. E is a bit scared and hurries out of the room.

INT. HISTORY CLASS

Chut is glaring at Alexis as she enters the room and takes her seat, but is annoyed and disappointed that she seems unaware that he's even there. There's a difference to her posture now as well, a bit more self-assured.

MR.HENCHER
Ok, ok settle down and we can begin...

Alexis' shoots up, she's got something to say. Everyone is a little surprised.

MR.HENCHER
um, yes Alexis?

ALEXIS
Can you tell us about George Washington Carver?

MR.HENCHER
uh, a bit random, but sure. George Washington Carver's research with peanuts revolutionized agriculture, promoting sustainability and creating new peanut-based products, leaving a lasting impact on farming.

ALEXIS
And what about Pickles?

MR.HENCHER
(confused) I'm not sure I follow...

ALEXIS
(relieved) Nevermind.

CHUT
(whispering for Alexis to hear) Weirdo.

MR.HENCHER
It's actually a good segue however into the next assignment. I'd like you to research a historical figure that has had an impact on your life today. So let's head to the library to start.

INT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL LIBRARY

Alexis is sitting at one of the research computers in the library. Other kid's are looking at books, writing things down. Chut and his crew are procrastinating. Chut has a straw and is tearing and crumpling a piece of paper, grinning like a mischievous idiot.

ALEXIS
(to herself) Hmmm, who should I research? Maybe someone who has something to do with stuffed animals? Maybe music? Or computers? Let's try computers!

Alexis types "historical figures behind computers" into the search bar and hits enter. The top entry is Ada Lovelace, inventor of the first computer algorithm.

ALEXIS
(to herself) Oooh, who's Ada Lovelace... inventor of the first computer algorithm...the Analytical Engine...in 1843? What? That's nuts!

Alexis leans back and it dawns on her...

ALEXIS
I could probably just go and meet her!

Chut makes his move, he fires his spitwad through the straw at Alexis. She effortlessly deflects it with her notebook. Chut is stunned and speechless.

ALEXIS
Oh grow up.

Alexis walks out of the library leaving Chut with his mouth open, unable to reply.

CHUT
(to himself) What's going on today?

INT. ALEXIS' BEDROOM

Alexis is standing next to Mags looking at the closed bedroom closet door. Mags is excited and seems to enjoy these adventures as much as Alexis.

ALEXIS
Ready Mags?

MAGS
(yes!) me-ow!

ALEXIS
Let's do it!

Alexis confidently opens the closet door, opens the small door at the back of the closet and jumps in head first, Mags right after.

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

ALEXIS
Alrighty, let's see if this works. Hotel? I want to go to London, England, 1843. I'd need some clothes too please!

Alexis and Mags wait expectantly and aren't disappointed, a breeze flows through the atrium and leads to an sturdy dark mahogany door with raised panels and flower motif.

ALEXIS
(looking to Mags) Yes!

EXT. EATON SQUARE, LONDON - 1843

Alexis opens the door and onto the street, wearing a bell-shaped dress with hoops and petticoats to support it. She's still wearing her signature sneakers though. She's walking a little awkwardly in the unfamiliar clothing, like an astronaut on the moon. Mags looks on in amusement.

The door opened at the top of some steps and Alexis is attempting to descend, but slips at the bottom and falls directly into a woman passing by, holding a leather portfolio filled with papers. They both fall to the ground and some of the papers come out.

ALEXIS
I'm so sorry! I tripped...

Both laughing, they pick up the scattered papers. Alexis glances at one of them, it's a chart with mathematical figures on it and at the bottom there are the initials A.A.L.

ALEXIS
(to herself) Ada Lovelace?

ADA
Yes? Have we met?

ALEXIS
Um, no, I'm just a fan.

ADA
A what?

ALEXIS
Sorry, I just know your work.

ADA
(smiling) You do?

They both start to stand up, Ada is sorting the papers back into the portfolio.

ALEXIS
Well... yeah... I'm kind of a computer...I mean, a math nerd, I mean, I'm interested in math and I've heard you're a good...math...person.

Alexis is totally flustered and Mags rolls her eyes.

ADA
(laughing and kindly correcting Alexis) I'm a mathematician, that's correct.

ALEXIS
What are these papers?

ADA
These? These are the operations or the calculus for an engine.

Alexis is lost and her face shows it. Mags is mirroring the expression.

ADA
(laughing) Walk with me and I can explain, I'm on the way to the Post.

Mags jumps on Alexis' shoulders and the three of them continue on, Alexis has a better grasp of how to move in the dress but it's not perfect.

ADA
Who's your friend?

ALEXIS
This is Mags.

ADA
Pleased to meet you Mags.

MAGS
Meow!

ADA
So, where to begin? Charles Babbage, another "good math person"...

Ada elbows Alexis in a friendly way.

ADA
...has built a machine, a calculating machine. These papers contain the instructions to allow it to compute a wide range of operations as well as perform multi-step operations.

ALEXIS
So instead of solving one problem at a time you can solve several, where the result of one can drive the next calculation?

ADA
You got it! Smart girl. I'm taking it to the post so it can be published and others can take the work even farther!

ALEXIS
That's rad! I mean, great!

Alexis and Ada have arrived at the post office and enter together.

INT. LONDON POST - 1843

As they enter Alexis looks around and sees, behind the counter, Six! He's got an even bigger fake moustache this time.

ALEXIS
You!

SIX
(in his fake older man voice) I don't... know what you might be... referring...

Six is flustered at being found out so quickly then gives up the rouse.

SIX
Ah forget it. Grab it E!

From behind Alexis and Ada, E grabs the portfolio in his mouth and jumps onto the counter and over it. Six smiles at Alexis.

SIX
Smell ya later!

Six and E abscond with the portfolio out the back door and into an alley. Alexis doesn't hesitate despite her unwieldly dress and hops over the counter and follows them into the alley with Mags close behind.

Ada is confused and standing at the post entrance still.

ADA
Smell you later? How odd.

INT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL COMPUTER LAB

We see the middle school computer lab and several students using them. Then suddenly there's a time glitch, the computers pop out of existence and abacuses drop into place. The sign that previously said "Computer Lab" now says "Abacus Lab". The teacher who was looking at his cell-phone is now looking at a small cell-phone-sized mini abacus. No one is at all aware that anything has happened.

EXT. ALLEYWAY BEHIND POST - 1843

Six and E are running ahead and Alexis and Mags are in pursuit. Now the dress is really getting in the way. She's really struggling to move. Six and E turn and notice that there is no danger of Alexis catching them.

ALEXIS
Next...time...pants!

Six takes the portfolio from E as they casually make their way to a red glowing door.

Above them, however, Mags has been jumping from window sill to window sill to get the drop on them. She's now in position, but waiting for the right moment.

E heads through the door and Six waves over-dramatically with the portfolio as he also goes through the doorway.

SIX
Better luck next...

In slow motion Six finally notices Mags but too late. Mags is flying towards him as the smile leaves his face. Mags, with her full weight, lands on the portfolio, knocking it out of his hands as he goes through the door fully, it closes soundly behind him.

INT. HOUSE OF EVERYWHERE

SIX
...time. AAAAARGH!!

EXT. ALLEYWAY BEHIND POST - 1843

Mags, sliding on the portfolio across the ground comes to a stop, looking proud.

Alexis, meanwhile has caught up and pushes a large crate that was sitting in the alley in front of the door, just in case.

ALEXIS
Nice one mags!

INT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL COMPUTER LAB

A time glitch hits the lab again, returning everything back to normal, with the exception of one computer which remains an abacus. The computer previously being used by Chut.

CHUT
What the...

INT. LONDON POST - 1843

Alexis and Mags reenter the post, Ada is explaining to a confused postmaster what had occurred.

ADA
...and the boy with the fake moustache, took my portfolio out the back...

ALEXIS
Here you go Ada.

ADA
Oh thank goodness!

POSTMASTER
(in a cockney accent) I was 'avin' me break, but it seems things are alright now, mum, yeah?

ADA
Indeed, but I think I'll deliver it myself. Thanks.

Alexis starts to make her way out the door.

ALEXIS
It was a pleasure meeting you Ada! Good luck with your Analytical Engine, I've got to run.

ADA
Thanks again clever girl!

INT. HISTORY CLASS

Mr.Hencher is handing back the graded papers. He's handing back Chut's paper, it has an A-.

MR.HENCHER
Excellent work Chut, well researched and well written. Richard Nixon was an...interesting choice...

Mr.Hencher's mildly confused look is replaced with a proud one as he hands Alexis' her A+ paper back.

MR.HENCHER
...and Alexis, yours felt, somehow, very personal. It really came alive, nice work!

Alexis is beaming.

INT. SANTIAGO KITCHEN

Eric, Martina and Alexis are sitting at the dinner table, the sun is setting and it's pizza night.

MARTINA
Soooo, how was everyone's week? Alexis, you want to go first?

ALEXIS
(between bites) My week was good.

ERIC
(jovially) A truly epic retelling Alexis. I was hanging on all four words.

MARTINA
psshh Eric, don't badger her.

ERIC
I do want to say though, Alexis, you seem a little different lately, more confident perhaps. Any reason?

Alexis puts down her slice and thinks for a moment.

ALEXIS
Actually, I feel a little different. Things have been, I don't know, more interesting.

MARTINA
That's great to hear.

ERIC
We're very proud of you Al.

ALEXIS
(bashfully) Thanks.

MARTINA
How are things with "Chut"?

Martina uses air quote and rolls her eyes.

ALEXIS
Honestly, he doesn't bother me much anymore. He tries to, but he just seems kind of small. I almost pity him.

ERIC
(between bites) I don't, kid's a grade A jerk and he's messin' with my girl...

Martina and Alexis look at Eric smiling.

ERIC
What? I'm your dad, I don't care if he's a kid, kid's can be jerks as well as anyone else. My priority is you kiddo...

Eric points at Alexis with his fork.

ALEXIS
(softly) Thanks dad.

INT. HOUSE OF EVERYWHERE

E is trying to sleep in the corner. Six is bouncing a ball off of a deteriorating wall.

SIX
(frustrated) She's always stopping me! I get so close to changing things, destablizing time, but at the last moment she and her cat interfere!

E
(in agreement) woof!

Six loses the ball through a hole in the wall and gives up the game. He bunches up some old clothes and blankets to go to sleep himself.

SIX
Goodnight E

E
Rowr

Six pulls the long string connected to the bare lightbulb in the center of the room. and the whole image goes to black.

EXT. LIGHTHOUSE BEACH - 1924

A nearby lighthouse search lamp wipes from the black frame to a dramatic stormy scene on a rocky beach. A somewhat younger Six and E are washed up on the shore, unconscious. Six has one arm around a life ring and one arm around E. They look like they’ve been through a rough time. The waves are still lapping at Six’ legs.

Suddenly, a door at the base of the nearby lighthouse opens, glowing with an eerie reddish glow.

THE VOID
(whispering) Come. Come to me boy. Get up.

Six is coming around, groggily, unsteadily.

SIX
Wha? Who’s there.

THE VOID
(speaking) Come boy, come to me, we can help each other, get up and out of the storm.

Six stumbles to his feet, dropping the life ring but still holding an unconscious E in his arms. The light of the doorway is growing brighter and the rest of the world darker and duller.

THE VOID
(loudly as if in our heads) Come, come now!

Six is silhouetted in the doorway, the light is blinding and the door slams shut.

INT. HOUSE OF EVERYWHERE

Six jolts awake, breathing hard and sweating, waking E too.

An intense dream, a memory. For a beat Six is reeling a bit from the emotions but is starting to calm down. Then he hears something and it’s giving him the creeps.

THE VOID
(from another room, in a sing-songy tone) Oh Six? Come here boy, we need to talk.

INT. THE VOID'S CHAMBER

Six and E enter the room, dejected and quite afraid.

THE VOID
Come in, come in. I know it didn't go as planned, it's alright.

Six and E are surprised and confused. They were expecting rage but the Void is weirdly calm and almost friendly sounding.

THE VOID
It's my fault, I've been pushing you too much, I see that. It's okay if you can't handle this girl. I understand.

Six doesn't appreciate the implication.

THE VOID
I know you love your family and that you are trying, but maybe...

Six is getting angry now.

THE VOID
...it's just not enough. If only I could fix my… situation… I could help them. If was free, you'd be reunited in no time, quite literally.

SIX
I can do it! Don't say that I can't!

THE VOID
(ignoring Six and speaking to itself) Maybe he just doesn't care as much as he says he does.

SIX
Of course I care! I love them, I would do anything for them!

Although it's a hole in the wall, the pause before the Void speaks again as well as the tone imply a manipulative smile, Six has fallen for it.

THE VOID
Oh dear boy, if you would do anything, well, then I think you know what has to happen to this meddling girl don't you?

Six realizes the implication of the Void's words, so does E who is growling at the Void.

SIX
(softly) I've got to stop her.

THE VOID
Stop her from meddling, ever again.

SIX
(whispering reluctantly) I know.

INT. ALEXIS' BEDROOM - NIGHT

Alexis is sitting on her bed looking at her laptop and absent mindedly scratching the belly of a purring Mags.

ALEXIS
What do you think Mags? Should we go back?

MAGS
(disinterested) mrrow

ALEXIS
You're right, probably not a good idea to mess with time.

MAGS
(still not really caring) mrrow

ALEXIS
Although, if we're careful, it could be quite educational, wouldn't you say?

MAGS
(ignoring Alexis)

ALEXIS
In fact, it's almost our responsibility to go, you know to make sure we really know how things happened.

MAGS
(realizing the scratches are ending) mrrow?

ALEXIS
Then we are in agreement, we must return. Off we go!

Mags reluctantly stands up and lazily stretches and is grabbed by Alexis mid-stretch and they dive into the closet together.

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

A giddy Alexis and a partially ready Mags are standing at the end of a long narrow hallway that branches off the main atrium. It's lined with doors of all types. Alexis is staring down the hall thinking.

ALEXIS
Where should we go? You know, I was reading earlier that quite a lot of our math comes from the students of Hypatia but none of her actual writings survived.

Alexis turns to Mags who is not really listening and cleaning her paws.

ALEXIS
What do you say, check out Alexandria, Egypt in the 5th century?

Mags could care less.

ALEXIS
I think I also read that they had some pretty great seafood.

MAGS
(looking up with full attention) Mrrrow?

The tell-tale wind starts blowing, directing them down the hall to an ancient looking wooden door with geometric patterns and ellipses drawn on it. They travel through.

INT. HYPATIA'S CLASSROOM - ALEXANDRIA, EGYPT - 5TH CENTURY

Alexis, wearing a linen tunic and cloak, quietly enters a large open room with an open ceiling, in which students are seated and listening to a woman speaking at the front of the room. Pointing to a model of planets on elliptical orbits. Alexis sneaks up to the other students and sits down to listen.

HYPATIA
...and in order to measure the distances of stars or the sun we can use this, an astrolabe.

Hypatia is holding an ornate device that looks like the inner workings of a clock. She holds it up for the students to see it and then holds it above herself and looks through one part of it, upwards.

HYPATIA
With this device one can align the device with a known point, such as Polaris, the north star, and measure the distances and paths of other cosmic bodies.

Alexis looks at the stars and imagines the paths of some of the stars, represented as dotted lines growing and filling in on top of the view of the ancient night sky, a sneak peek at what Alexis is visualizing in her mind.

ALEXIS
(whispering) Beautiful!

Even Mags is struck by the incredibly clear view of the night sky, the Milky Way is even visible.

INT. HOUSE OF EVERYWHERE

Six and E are standing in the foyer of the House of Everywhere, there is a similar barometer-looking device hanging where a chandelier might have typically been.

The barometer is flickering but Six doesn't notice. He's distracted, thinking about what the void was implying.

E, however, notices the barometer and is pulling at Six's pant leg to get his attention.

SIX
Sorry E, I need to focus, just let me think for a minute.

E rolls his eyes and barks instead. That snaps Six out of it and he follows E's eyeline to the barometer.

SIX
What's happening? Is she out there messing with the timeline?

E
(confirming Six suspicion) Woof!

SIX
Ha! Looks like she might be doing our job for us! Maybe we could track her...

the house creaks and shifts in response, dried leaves and dust blowing leads our view to a very similar door as the one we saw Alexis travel through.

SIX
(continuing)...down? Come on E, let's go!

INT. HYPATIA'S CLASSROOM - ALEXANDRIA, EGYPT - 5TH CENTURY

Six and E enter the classroom and see Alexis and Mags sitting in the back, but they stick to the shadows, watching.

The lecture concludes and Alexis walks over to Hypatia.

ALEXIS
That was brilliant, thank you for the lesson.

HYPATIA
You're welcome, child.

ALEXIS
Come on Mags, let's get back. Where to next?

MAGS
Mrrow

ALEXIS
First flight it is!

Six and E are still lurking in the shadows, listening and waiting as Alexis walks past and through the door leading back to the Hotel Nowhere.

As the door is just about to close, Six sticks out his foot stopping it from shutting and he and E slip inside after her.

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

Six is stunned by what he sees, this place is much more elaborate than the House of Everywhere. He manages to stay quiet though and sees Alexis and Mags just heading through another door that looks like it's made of barn wood.

There's no time to really look at the hotel, they make it just in time to get through the door following Alexis.

EXT. KITTY HAWK, NORTH CAROLINA - DECEMBER 17TH, 1903

Alexis and Mags are standing in a small crowd, excitedly waiting for the Wright brothers to launch the first flight.

Six pulls out an especially large moustache and works his way over to Wilbur and Orville Wright as they are doing some final checks on their aircraft.

SIX
(in a fake-adult-old-timey voice) I say, there's something the matter with that thing-a-ma-jig there on the left side of your craft.

The brothers pause and look at this odd gentleman addressing them and both look at the flying machine where Six indicated, to make sure all was in order.

While they are distracted Six duct tapes a rock to the underside of the right side wing, unbalancing the machine in a subtle but important way.

SIX
Perhaps I was mistaken. I might have had a few too many of Mr. Graham's crackers, if you know what I mean.

Six, gently elbows Wilbur knowingly. The brothers are supremely annoyed and confused by this odd moustached fellow.

SIX
Toodles!

Six is snickering as he walks away with E and the brothers return to their mission.

A moment later, Orville was climbing into the Wright Flyer, getting ready to launch.

WILBUR WRIGHT
Ready?

ORVILLE WRIGHT
Ready.

WILBUR WRIGHT
On your mark...get set...

EXT. SKY - 2024

A 747 is flying through the air with a full passenger load. Suddenly, a time glitch and the plane disappears. The passengers are all still in a sitting position, a man is reading a paper, a woman is eating a sandwich, the pilot is in the front, in uniform but she and all the rest don't realize anything is wrong.

After a beat they start to lose their momentum and start to fall, yet are still not reacting to the situation.

EXT. KITTY HAWK, NORTH CAROLINA - DECEMBER 17TH, 1903

ALEXIS
Wait!

Wilbur stops before saying “go” and looks at Alexis. Orville is anxiously waiting and looking at her too. The whole small crowd has turned to her and are waiting to see what's happening.

Alexis runs over to the flyer. It's a bit of a distance and she's fighting the long skirt she's wearing to blend in. Everyone is silently watching her, like a slow motion tennis match and she's the ball.

She finally arrives at the flyer, pulls off the rock she saw taped underneath the right side wing. Then running back to her original position in the crowd.

ALEXIS
Proceed!

WILBUR WRIGHT
as I was saying...Go!

The flyer successfully coasts through the air.

EXT. SKY - 2024

Just as suddenly as it had disappeared, the airplane reappears, slightly lower in frame to account for the falling people, but then corrects and returns to the proper cruising distance.

A food cart however didn't make it back into the plane and falls out of frame.

EXT. PUBLIC PARK - 2024

A view of a peaceful park, an older man, Stanley, is feeding some birds from a park bench, overlooking a small pond.

There is a falling whistling sound from above and off screen building and getting louder. Then CRASH! The airplane food cart is embedded in the grass, jammed into the ground at a funny angle.

STANLEY
Jeepers!

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

Alexis and Mags are heading towards the small homeward door, looking tired from their experiences. Behind them, the barometer is looking a little off and it's jittering slightly.

MAGS
(worriedly) meow

ALEXIS
You're right Mags, that doesn't quite look right. Let's get some sleep and maybe try looking into that tomorrow after school.

INT. HOUSE OF EVERYWHERE

Six and E, yet again unsuccessful in their efforts, are trying to sneak down the hall and past the attic door leading to the void.

THE VOID
(in a loud commanding tone) STOP.

The two freeze, caught, steeling themselves for when comes next.

THE VOID
Enter.

Six in a defeated posture and E in a tense defensive one enter the Void's chamber. Bracing themselves.

THE VOID
It's working!

Six opens one eye, surprised by this turn of events.

THE VOID
I can feel the barriers of time weakening. Whatever you are doing, it's working.

SIX
But...we failed to disrupt the timeline.

THE VOID
I can't explain it, but perhaps the back and forth between you and the girl is enough to destabilize the barrier that keeps me imprisoned, from my freedom.

Six is now more comfortable and E has relaxed as well.

SIX
And then you can save my family?

THE VOID
Yes, yes, that too.

E isn't pleased by that tone, but Six seems satisfied.

EXT. SUBURBAN NEIGHBORHOOD

Alexis is walking to school, headphones on and walking confidently to the beat of her upbeat music. Alexis is in profile as the camera follows along, the houses pass in the background, cars and people on the opposite side of the street passing in the foreground.

One of the gray cookie cutter houses glitches and turns neon pink. Alexis doesn't lose a step and keeps going but her head does turn curiously towards it as she passes.

ALEXIS
...interesting...

Alexis continues, a man in the foreground is mowing his lawn then after Alexis passes, out of her view, he glitches and disappears.

Another house has all it's Christmas decorations up and it's covered in snow although it's the middle of summer. Alexis continues onwards but a bit slower, looking at the house.

ALEXIS
...something...isn't...

A woman riding a horse-sized Chihuahua gallops by. Alexis stops mid-stride. The music she's listening to slows like someone put their hand on a vinyl record.

ALEXIS
...right here.

Alexis, knowing she might be the source of this weirdness, pivots on her heel and then heads straight home, double time!

INT. ALEXIS' BEDROOM

Alexis rushes into her room, closing the door and the weird world behind her. Then she looks into her room, to see Mags, wide-eyed, on the bed staring at the stuffed animals in the room that are floating as if in zero gravity.

ALEXIS
Eeep! With me Mags, we've got to fix this somehow.

They jump in the closet without hesitation.

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

Alexis and Mags look up and see the barometer looking much worse than when we last saw it. It's glitching and changing levels and colors.

ALEXIS
That's not good. It must be that kid! Hotel! I need to undo what that boy has been doing!

The breeze, much stronger and almost stormier than before, takes her to a door. It's a sturdy oak door with old German printed lettering on the door. Without much thought, they pop through.

INT. MAINZ, GERMANY - 1440

Alexis walks into a room with a large printing press. A sign by the door in large German-style script says "Gutenberg". A man is trying to fix a broken printing press.

INT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL LIBRARY

Several kids are walking around and reading books in the school library, suddenly all of the books transform into papyrus scrolls. One large scroll rolls past, unrolling as it travels, a young boy is desperately trying to catch it.

INT. MAINZ, GERMANY - 1440

Alexis grabs the wrench out of Johannes Gutenberg's hand and quickly adjusts some things. She hands it back to him, gives him a funny salute and slaps the press to get it running again. Alexis and Mags then leave as quickly as they came.

INT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL LIBRARY

All the scrolls turn back into normal books. The boy who was chasing the scroll stops and looks confused as to why he's standing where he is.

INT. SERVER ROOM, CERN - 1989

Six is switching cables around randomly and with glee in a server room next to Tim Berners-Lee's office, inventor of the World Wide Web.

INT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL COMPUTER LAB

All of the computers change from having wifi and thin ethernet cables to a complex mess of large pipes and tubes networking them all together. One child seems to be trapped by them at the edge of the room.

INT. SERVER ROOM, CERN - 1989

Mags is reading a big thick manual filled with complex diagrams while Alexis is replugging the cables back in the correct location.

MAGS
(knowingly) Meow

ALEXIS
Got it. Ok, next one?

MAGS
Meow meow.

ALEXIS
Ok, next?

INT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL COMPUTER LAB

The computer lab returns to normal and the previously trapped child runs out the door.

INT. WARSAW, POLAND - 1829

Alexis and Mags burst into a room, exhausted from chasing after Six and E. They find Six talking with a 19-year old Frédéric Chopin and handing him an 80's Casio synthesizer and smiling at Alexis. She's out of breath and has her hands on her knees panting and can't say anything just yet.

Chopin turns it on and plays a really synthy sounding chord.

CHOPIN
That's lovely!

He presses another button and a cheesy preprogrammed drum loop plays. They all sit motionless in this room listening to the beat for a moment.

Chopin is clearly thinking, inspiration is about to hit him. He proceeds to play a really funky switched-on version of Waltz in B Minor.

ALEXIS
That's actually pretty great.

MAGS
(in agreement) mrrow.

ALEXIS
Let this one slide? What could it hurt?

INT. ALEXIS' BEDROOM - MORNING

It's quiet and calm. No stuffed animals are floating. Alexis and Mags are still in their clothes, sprawled across the bed, sleeping the sleep of the righteous.

Alexis is waking, groggily, stretching and yawning.

ALEXIS
(yawning) I think we did it Mags. I think we fixed it all.

MAGS
(without opening her eyes) mrrow

ALEXIS
Go ahead and sleep in Mags, you earned it.

INT. SANTIAGO KITCHEN

Alexis enters the kitchen to join her parents for breakfast, but not looking up yet.

ALEXIS
Good morning parental units!

ERIC
Gnarly morning, to the max, to you too kiddo.

Alexis looks up to see her parents wearing matching silver windbreakers with hot pink and teal accents. They've got on yellow framed triangular sunglasses. Beyond the kitchen the living room is also 80's retro futuristic. Out the front window a futuristic DeLorean-esque hover car floats by blasting synthwave pop music.

Alexis is stunned and her parents are staring at her, trying to understand her facial expression. It's caught somewhere between horror, shock and amusement. A moment later her expression resolves to pure joy.

ALEXIS
(in a low voice) This...is...AWESOME!

Her parents are pleasantly surprised and go back to breakfast as usual.

ALEXIS
(to herself) Can I leave it like this? I want to leave it like this. Can I do that? I think I probably can't, can I? I should fix this. I don't want to fix it...ugh...

MARTINA
Everything ok dear?

Alexis' parents are staring at her again, the orange juice her mother is pouring is in danger of over filling the glass

ALEXIS
(to noone in particular) FINE! I'll fix it! Argh, can't I have anything nice...razza frazza \*unintelligible grumbling noises\*

Alexis storms upstairs again. Her parents are still frozen trying to process what's happening and the orange juice glass is now overflowing.

INT. WARSAW, POLAND - 1829

Alexis marches into Chopin's room, he's sleeping and the keyboard is sitting on a table. She flips it over, takes out the batteries and slams it back down on the table as she marches back out of the room.

CHOPIN
(groggily) Hello?

Alexis is already gone and Chopin is alone.

INT. SANTIAGO KITCHEN

Alexis is sitting at the normal breakfast table with her arms crossed. Her mom is reading the newspaper and her dad is making eggs, oblivious to her thoughts.

ALEXIS
(to herself) ...probably for the best.

INT. NEWTON MIDDLE SCHOOL HALLWAY

Alexis is on autopilot with her headphones on. Boring normal school day. Chut is in the background being his normal loud and pompous self with his crew. They seem so small and silly now.

We see Alexis, center frame closeup, we are traveling with her and looking down the hall.

Chut is mansplaining something when, midsentence, his clothing and hair style glitch and now he's wearing an 1800's tweed suit and bowler cap. No one, including Chut notices.

A tall lanky girl is crossing the frame behind Alexis and suddenly switches to futuristic silver clothing and cyberpunk goggles.

Alexis is still unaware but the music she is listening to starts to build, getting darker and more intense and rhythmically glitchy. She continues down the hall.

Two boys are chatting by an open locker door. The boy with glasses glitches and is now a lizard person wearing the same outfit and glasses. The boys continue to joke around naturally.

The locker doors start glitching and become wooden cabinets.

In one portion of an adjacent hall it's becoming overgrown with trees and vines.

A young girl is floating across the hall behind Alexis and uses lasers fired from her eyes to vaporize the classroom door before floating in.

Alexis starts to react to the changes in her music and a sense that something is happening behind her, she pulls the headphones down around her neck and turns to look.

She's stunned by the absolute madness that was previously Newton Middle School. Everything is in a state of flux, reality seems to be malfunctioning today.

Alexis recovers her wits and realizes this must be related to her time adventures and takes off to try and fix things if she can.

INT. SANTIAGO KITCHEN

Alexis bursts into the kitchen to find her mother and father sitting at the kitchen table drinking tea. Her father is in full Viking warrior gear including face paint and her mother is wearing a Stola in the ancient Rome style.

MARTINA
(in Latin) iam domum es? vis aliqua tea? (translation: You're home already? Want some tea?)

ALEXIS
huh?

ERIC
(in Old Norse) Ert þú allr? (translation: Are you okay?)

ALEXIS
I...can't even...

Without saying anything further Alexis bolts upstairs and into her room, back against the closed door, breathing hard and looking terrified.

INT. ALEXIS' BEDROOM

Alexis' terror increases as she sees her room, it's in the process of glitching into a sterile minimalist environment. Her books and figures are disappearing and her beloved stuffed animals are turning into weird boring decorative cubes. She grabs her special curry-stained bunny in an attempt to save it but it turns into a cube in her hand.

ALEXIS
AAAH! Dr.Hopps!

MAGS
(muffled) mrrrow

ALEXIS
Mags! Where are you?

Mags is pushing her way out of the pile of cubes she's found herself under. Alexis runs over and pushes them aside and scooping Mags up into her arms.

ALEXIS
I'm so glad you're ok, everything is such a mess. It's all my fault.

MAGS
(disagreeing adamantly) Mrrow!

ALEXIS
(deterimined) You're right, it's not my fault at all. I was trying to fix it. It's that boy and his dog!

MAGS
(satisfied) Mrrow.

ALEXIS
Let's get 'em!

Alexis and Mags dive into the closet.

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

As Alexis enters the atrium it's immediately clear that something is not right with the hotel. There's an irregular rumbling and the sound of an enormous structure creaking and straining. The barometer is looking supremely unhealthy, impossible to read the status as it's in constant flux. All of the doors are rattling and glowing slightly.

Alexis looks panicked and his holding Mags tightly. Mags is also scared. This is a bad situation and Alexis is not in good shape.

Then, a moment of realization, Alexis closes her eyes. The sounds and the chaos of the Hotel are softer, calming. Alexis breaths in an out and that's all we hear now.

INT. ALEXIS' HEAD

Alexis opens her eyes and she's in a dark space with Mags.

MAGS
mrrow?

ALEXIS
I think this is my mind. I don't think I've got super powers or anything, I think you're just a representation of Mags to help my orientation.

MAGS
(satisfied with that answer) mew.

ALEXIS
(narrating to herself) I struggle with a lot of small things, things other people do easily. But you know what? I am awesome at big things!

Alexis turns and starts to see the Pickens Motel fade in, replacing the darkness. Our view is spinning but Alexis is stationary in the center of frame.

ELVIS
That's right kid!

The Motel fades away and is replaced with the 1921 Capitol Building and George Washington Carver is there.

ALEXIS
I've traveled through time! I've defended it!

CARVER
You did!

Still spinning, a bit faster, the Capitol Building fades into London and Ada Lovelace is there.

ALEXIS
I'm a guardian of the timeline and with my wits and cunning I can fix this.

ADA
You sure can!

Even faster, London gives way to Alexandria, Egypt.

HYPATIA
You've got this!

Alexandria gives way to Kittyhawk.

ALEXIS
I can fix ANYTHING when I put my mind to it!

ORVILLE WRIGHT
You betcha'!

Kittyhawk fades into Chopin's room, the spinning is at maximum now.

CHOPIN
(in Polish) Dajesz!

Alexis closes her eyes within her mind...

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

...and opens them in the Hotel Nowhere. Alexis has a confident and determined look on her face. The Hotel is still buzzing with energy but now it's more high frequency, focused, awaiting the actions of Alexis.

A closeup on Alexis' face, a beat of calm before the storm. Her game face is on!

ALEXIS
Let's do this!

A big door in the center of the atrium, below the barometer, blasts open, coursing with energy and light, silhouetting Alexis as she and Mags stand on the precipice.

INT. HOUSE OF EVERYWHERE

The chaos we witnessed in the Hotel Nowhere was nothing compared to the quakes that are ripping through the House of Everywhere. The walls are heaving and cracking, dust and debris falling from the ceiling.

SIX
(terrified) What's going on?!

E
awooooo!

SIX
Come on, let’s move!

Six and E, with no other options head toward the attic to consult the Void. In the confusion and chaos, neither notice the door opening in the foyer of the bizarro mansion.

Alexis and Mags enter, just in time to see which way Six and E are heading and they give chase, no hesitation.

ALEXIS
Let's go!

INT. THE VOID'S CHAMBER

Six and E run into the Void's chamber and come to a sudden stop. This room seems to be the epicenter of the chaos, the Void being the dead center.

THE VOID
(laughing) Finally! Finally!

SIX
What's going on? What's happening?

THE VOID
The barrier is weakening, I can feel it! I can break through! Finally I'll be free of this prison.

An energy surge pulses through the walls, the hole that houses the void is growing, spider-web-like cracks spreading all around.

Six looks at E. His eyes are watering from the extreme emotions.

SIX
E, you know what this means? We can save my family, we can go home!

But even now, Six isn't sure he believes it. This doesn't feel right, it feels dangerous.

THE VOID
(laughing maniacally) Ha ha ha! Nothing will stop me! Reality will bend to my will!

SIX
(nervously) What about my family, you'll help them right? You promised!

A massive pulse shakes the room nearly knocking Six over. As he regains his footing, he sees Alexis and Mags in the doorway watching. They've been witness to the whole exchange.

Alexis has a look of fear and of empathy for Six on her face, she realizes he's not some kind of villain after all.

The room is shaking with enormous energy, but it's getting more and more focused and feeding directly to the center of the Void. Objects in the room start to float, including Alexis and Six, as if gravity was also being sucked into the void. There's a screaming high pitched sound followed by a sharp crack!

Everything falls to the ground, the room stops shaking and silence.

Alexis and Six sit up, confused and scared, powerless to do anything but stare into the void.

There's a subtle scratching sound and a tiny pitter patter of feet.

A small guinea pig trots out of the gaping hole in the wall and into the center of the room and sits down. There is a natural looking but distinctly horizontal figure-eight shape in the coloring of the guinea pig's fur, an infinity symbol.

For a moment all anyone can do is just stare incredulously.

THE VOID
(the void actually meaning the guinea pig, speaking with the same menacing voice) Not what you expected eh?

SIX
I'm at a loss here.

THE VOID
It's expected.

Alexis stands up and dusts herself off. Mags starts to clean herself.

ALEXIS
Hamster or not, you broke time!

THE VOID
(annoyed) Guinea Pig. I'm not a filthy hamster.

ALEXIS
(genuinely) Oh, sorry. But still, time! You broke it! Why?

THE VOID
Time. Time time time time time. You might feel differently about time if you'd experienced as much of it as I have.

SIX
What do you mean?

EXT. TEMPORAL LAB - 1963

Deep in a remote jungle we see a 1960's style building with a single two-track road leading to it. The building is a big rectangular and windowless monolithic compound. There's a big circular sign with a corporate logo in the shape of an infinity symbol mounted on the wall.

We see a small non-descript light gray metal door with lettering on it stating "Temporal Lab B".

INT. TEMPORAL LAB - 1963

A scientist wearing a lab coat and big black rubber gloves and a black rubber apron enters a lab pushing a cart. On the top of the cart is a guinea pig with the same distinct shape on it's back.

THE VOID
(narrating) At one point in time, I was just a normal happy guinea pig.

We see the scientist place the guinea pig in a big maze.

THE VOID
Well, not totally normal, I was the best. I could solve the mazes that the others couldn't...

The guinea pig makes it out of the maze and is rewarded with a big leafy carrot. The scientist is pleased.

THE VOID
...I had excellent endurance...

The guinea pig is running in a "hamster wheel" attached to various sensors and cables while the scientist looks on, taking notes, satisfied.

THE VOID
...and incredible agility!

The guinea pig is in a clear plastic "hamster ball" and deftly navigating an unusually dangerous obstacle course with moving blocks, big hammers and flame throwers. The scientist is cheering now!

THE VOID
After passing all of their tests, training endless hours, meeting every little bit of criteria they could muster...

The scientist wheels the cart into a new more ominous room. It's dimly lit and at one end of the room is a big circular techno hoop mounted on the wall. It's fed by giant python-like cables and clearly the main feature of the room.

The scientist types something into a 1960's style terminal and the room starts to hum. He wheels the cart near the mouth of the techno-hoop then pushes a switch with a lot of resistance. The hoop comes to life, crackling with energy and in the center a blackhole-like portal is opening, blasting wind and energy into the room.

The scientist picks up the guinea pig gently, petting it to calm the scared creature.

THE VOID
...and they just threw me away like I was garbage.

The scientist unceremoniously tosses the poor animal directly into the hoop. Once through, the whole mechanism shuts down and the room lights come on. The scientist casually writes something on his notepad, heads out the door, turns off the lights and shuts the door.

INT. THE VOID - 400 MILLION YEARS AGO

A terrified guinea pig is floating in blackness.

THE VOID
I didn't know what was happening, where I was, nothing. I didn't know to even ask myself WHEN I was, but that would be answered soon enough.

The guinea pig is still floating but now half of the blackness is replaced with a primordial scene, our world.

THE VOID
I had traveled through time, 400 million years into the past...

As the camera pans around the guinea pig we see that the primordial scene and the dark empty blackness are divided like looking through the glass at an infinitely large aquarium. The guinea pig is floating in the black half looking towards the primordial world.

There's a shallow greenish pool of water and an early fish-like creature with amphibian features is struggling out of the muddy water onto land. It's gasping and it's eyes are awkwardly looking all around, trying to focus, reeling from the new experience.

The guinea pig is looking on in awe, helpless but interested.

THE VOID
...to witness one of my earliest ancestors. It was magical and my little brain was just taking it all in.

INT. THE VOID - 300 MILLION YEARS AGO

Still in the divided void, but the primordial world is now covered in trees, more confident amphibians and lizards are walking around as well as insects and spiders.

THE VOID
At first, it was stunning, but soon I realized I was trapped. I was trapped at the edge of an endless void, a witness to time itself. I didn't age, I didn't go hungry, I was beyond time, out of it's grasp. I also was helpless. I was going mad.

INT. THE VOID - 7 MILLION YEARS AGO

A world of dense forests in the distance and open grasslands in the foreground, we see some very early apes starting to stand, our first branch towards humans.

THE VOID
But then, a memory, one I had thought long forgotten, was triggered.

We see the moment of realization on the floating guinea pig's face.

The camera is focused on the mouth of the guinea pig as it whispers it's first word.

THE VOID
Humans.

INT. THE VOID - TIMELAPSE

The early Savanna environment transitions into rapidly changing images, a timelapse of human civilization, our greatest hits.

We see the key moments reflected on the widening eyes of the guinea pig. Early humans working with stone tools and using fire, agriculture developing in the Fertile Crescent, first cities developing in Mesopotamia, pyramids in Egypt, iron forges in the Hittite empire, rise and fall of Roman and Chinese Empires, the Renaissance , industrial revolution, and the development of computers.

THE VOID
I saw it all, the entirety of human civilization, I learned everything I could for two reasons. So that I might find a way through this barrier...

INT. THE VOID'S CHAMBER

We return to the attic chamber with Alexis, Six, E and Mags watching and listening intently to the guinea pig that was previously a void. Their expressions are a mix of terror and intrigue.

THE VOID
...by destabilizing time, thanks to you both.

SIX
What's the other reason?

Six and Alexis are a bit more relaxed now, as it seems the threat is gone and they are only facing a small guinea pig.

THE VOID
Why, REVENGE of course!

Before anyone can react, the guinea pig has a glowing aura and starts floating in the air, the room is once again energized and everything and everyone is floating menacingly. The room itself seems to be coming apart at the seams.

THE VOID
(maniacally) Ha ha ha ha ha!

SIX
How do you have superpowers?

THE VOID
A little witchcraft and science picked up over the millennia. Mwoo ha ha ha!

SIX
Oh… makes sense I guess.

Alexis grabs the nearby arm of Six and pulls him closer.He's still staring stunned at the floating nuclear guinea pig.

ALEXIS
(softly) follow me.

Six snaps out of his trance and grabs E by the scruff of his neck and the four of them using the floating objects as leverage make their way out of the attic chamber room.

Once out of the room, gravity seems to be more or less normal again. They can hear the Void cackling away as it unravels reality behind them. Ahead they see the open door that Alexis arrived through.

ALEXIS
There! Go through that door!

They are running as fast as they can, but fighting the cackling sucking blackhole behind them. He see the strained face of Six, tears streaming backwards off of his face.

SIX
I didn't know, I'm so sorry...

ALEXIS
No time for that now! Let's get out of here.

Alexis looks at his face, he's racked with guilt.

ALEXIS
It's alright, I understand. It's going to be fine.

Six, is surprised and even a tiny bit relieved to hear these words. He focuses and redoubles is efforts. He grabs E, Mags and Alexis and is pushing them all forward with herculean effort against the enormous sucking pressure.

There's nearly nothing left behind them, just scraps of the floor and the door in front of them.

SIX
Al...most...

They're all screaming and fighting for every inch.

SIX
THERE!

At the last possible moment they make it through and the door slams shut and into splinters.

EXT. SUBURBAN NEIGHBORHOOD

The chaotic surreal world that Alexis left behind is still madness. Stanley,the now elderly man, who has been witness to a lifetime of weird time glitches and is himself unaffected by the glitching time problems,is watching it all unfold with a blank expression on his face. That expression changes to a smirk. He's been validated.

STANLEY
I knew I wasn't crazy! See! It's just like I always said. I'm not crazy!

He stops for a moment, looking at the insanity surrounding him.

STANLEY
Or...maybe I really am.

Stanley looks defeated, but can't wallow in that feeling for long. A giant blackhole vortex is forming in the sky above the neighborhood.

We zoom way way way in to the massive disturbance to see at the center, a cackling guinea pig.

THE VOID
Bow before me! I am the master of reality! I will destroy this world and make one of my own design!

INT. SANTIAGO FRONT LAWN

Eric and Martina are standing on the front lawn looking up at the mayhem. Eric is still a viking and Martina is still dressed as if from ancient Rome.

Eric shakes his axe at the heavens.

ERIC
(in old Norse) Far þú í burt, illr kvikindi! (Translation: Go away foul beast!)

INT. HOTEL NOWHERE

Although Alexis, Mags, Six and E have made it to the Hotel Nowhere, they are still not safe, the door they came through has imploded into nothing and a small hole in reality is left in it's place and it's growing.

Panicked, they are looking around at the shaking Hotel, grasping for any idea on what to do.

SIX
This is all my fault. I knew messing with time was dangerous, I just would do anything to get my family back.

ALEXIS
You couldn't have known. I played my part in this as well, but it does no good to think that way.

MAGS
(in agreement) mrrow

E
(in agreement) woof

ALEXIS
If we get through this, I will do whatever I can to help you.

Six nods in appreciation.

ALEXIS
But what to do? It's all so broken, if only we didn't mess with time in the first place.

SIX
In the first place. hmm in the first place.

Mags and E look at each other, implying they don't know what the humans are getting at.

ALEXIS & SIX
(in unison) We need to go to the beginning!

A door opposite of them opens.

EXT. TEMPORAL LAB - 1963

We're back in 1963, except this time it's not a flashback. We see the same building as we had before.

INT. TEMPORAL LAB - 1963

Alexis, Six, Mags and E pop through the main door in the lab just as the scientist is about to toss the guinea pig into the portal.

ALEXIS & SIX
STOP!

The scientist is startled but freezes. He collects himself and turns off the machine and gently sets the guinea pig back on the cart. Then prepares to listen to the visitors.

ALEXIS
I know it sounds crazy, but we're from the future!

SIX
What you're about to do will have tragic consequences...

The scientist calmly puts his hand up gesturing they should stop talking.

Alexis and Six stop themselves mid-sentence, this is less dramatic than they had anticipated.

SCIENTIST
So you're from the future, this temporal experiment I'm about to perform is going to have tragic consequences. Got it.

Alexis and Six look at each other, somewhat confused.

The scientist points at the wall behind him, there is a poster, on it is written instructions on how to deal with time travelers.

SCIENTIST
We’ve got procedures for situations like this. It’s not the first time this has happened.

SIX
What’s the procedure?

The scientist pulls out a thick three ring binder and starts looking through it.

SCIENTIST
Let’s see… ok, so chapter 3…uh huh, yes, ok…see subparagraph 27b/6…

Alexis and Six are almost bored now, it’s taking quite a while for the scientist to locate the right part.

SCIENTIST
Here it is! If time travelers from the future come to warn you about the experiment you are about to perform…

ALEXIS & SIX
(in unison) What does it say?!

SCIENTIST
Huh, it simply says “Believe them” and then it says I should destroy the experiment immediately.

ALEXIS & SIX
(in unison) Really?

SCIENTIST
Yes. Very well. Thanks for the warning.

The scientist pulls a lever and the whole portal machine starts shaking and sparking and then almost instantaneously implodes in on itself and a tiny dense metal cube falls to the floor. The scientist goes over, picks it up, put’s it into a clear plastic back labeled “Rejected”, brings it over to a pneumatic tube in the corner, puts it in the receptacle, pushes a big red button and it gets sucked through the tube out of the room.

ALEXIS
That’s it?

SCIENTIST
That’s it. Will you manage to see yourselves out or back to your time or dimension?

ALEXIS
(still a bit incredulous) Um, yeah I think we’re good.

SCIENTIST
Very well, good day.

The scientist begins wheeling the cart out of the room. Alexis suddenly jerks to attention.

ALEXIS
Wait! We’re taking the guinea pig!

SCIENTIST
You’re taking Agatha? If you must. She likes carrots by the way.

Alexis runs over and grabs Agatha, holding her close, not wanting to risk anything. Alexis is feeling like this was all too easy and has a very skeptical look on her face.

ALEXIS
Well…ok then… good day to you as well sir.

The scientist nods and leaves the room, shutting the door behind him.

SIX
Hey, uh, let’s get out of here.

ALEXIS
Good call.

They all head for the door which is glowing in the old familiar way.

EXT. SUBURBAN NEIGHBORHOOD

Everything is as we left it last time, total mayhem. The Void is still in the sky cackling away.

THE VOID
Nothing can st…

Mid sentence, the Void stops, her eyes go wide. We see in her eyes the reflection of the timeline of human civilization, but in reverse. It continues back even to the point of being thrown in the portal then stops. The view pulls out to reveal a happy looking guinea pig, Agatha, being cradled in Alexis’ arms. Mags is a little bit skeptical but will allow it.

The full crew, Alexis, Mags, Six, E and now Agatha are safely back in the Hotel Nowhere which is as good as new. The barometer looks totally healthy.

ALEXIS
We did it!

SIX
I would say **you** did it.

ALEXIS
(proudly) That’s actually correct, I did!

SIX
What happens now?

ALEXIS
(smiling) What did the Void promise you again?

EXT. FAMILY LOST AT SEA - 1924

A small wooden fishing trawler, about 60 feet in length, is bobbing wildly in a tremendous storm. Massive waves are heaving the boat up and down. In the wheelhouse of the boat is a tough looking sailor woman with dark hair, battling with the wheel, she’s being assisted by young man with the same dark hair, Six’s mother and older brother. Holding on desperately is a somewhat younger looking Six.

A door swings open in the wheelhouse and Six’s father, a burly red headed man enters. He gives Six a wink, but clearly is troubled by the severity of the storm. He tosses a life ring to the young Six then helps with the wheel as well. A lighthouse is barely visible in the distance, hardly helpful against this storm.

We see out in front, a truly epic wave building and building. Time is almost standing still as the ship slides reluctantly up its side.

The terror on their faces is in full view now.

Then the wave breaks and crashes down on the ship, breaking the window and washing Six out the door screaming. The rest of his family have held on but Six has gone over the edge of the ship‘s deck.

Eleanor, Six’s mother, is the first to react and runs out on the ship’s deck, held back only by her husband, William and her elder son, Edward.

ELEANOR
(in anguish) Six! My sweet boy!

But in this very dark moment, suddenly from behind this grief stricken family, a light is shining. Standing in the doorway to the wheelhouse is Six coming from a door within the Hotel. The storm is still raging around the boat but the sound is somehow muted now.

Six is trying to control all of his mixed emotions, he’s ecstatic but tears are streaming down his face. He holds out a hand towards his family.

SIX
Mom? Dad? Eddie? It’s ok. I made it.

WILLIAM
I…I don’t understand…

SIX
It’s alright, just come with me, all of you come with me.

INT. SANTIAGO LIVING ROOM

Alexis, Six, Mags, E, Six’s parents and brother are standing in the Santiago living room while Alexis’s parents, Eric and Martina are sitting on the couch, trying to understand what is being explained to them. Seemingly it’s been a long and complex explanation.

ALEXIS
…so we saved the guinea pig…

SIX
Agatha.

ALEXIS
Right, we saved Agatha, saved Six’s family from a doomed fishing vessel in 1924…

SIX
Hi, I’m six and this E and my family.

SIX'S FAMILY
(awkwardly) Ahoy?

Eric and Martina‘s eyes dart around looking at each person who’s speaking, but otherwise totally motionless. Martina is holding a tea cup in the air but neither drinking it nor putting it down.

ALEXIS
We fixed time, I think, and put everything back the way it’s supposed to be, temporally speaking.

SIX
Well, we did pull my family from the past…

ALEXIS
Right, we did do that, but, of course we had to. And that’s whats been going on.

Alexis is wincing, preparing herself for whatever reaction her parents will have, it’s a total unknown for her.

There’s a couple beats of awkward silence as everyone in the room is trying to be cordial and sort through the weirdness.

ERIC
That…is a lot…it’s truly amazing, but it’s a lot.

MARTINA
We’re, of course, incredibly proud that you saved reality and time and whatnot.

SIX
(awkwardly interjecting) She really did! She’s pretty amazing.

ERIC
(genuinely) We’re really proud of you Al.

Alexis stops wincing and realizes it’s actually ok.

ALEXIS
And, you believe me?

ERIC AND MARTINA
Of course.

ERIC
You never lie to us Al, we trust you.

ALEXIS
So what happens now?

ERIC
Well, Six and his family are welcome to stay with us for now, and uh, we’ll, uh…um…

MARTINA
We’ll figure it out dear, together.

Everyone is visibly relieved. Things are going to be fine.

INT. STANLEY'S APARTMENT

Stanley is sitting on his couch with his head in his hands. The room is scattered with all kinds of strange objects, things we recognize like the airplane cart, the jar of pickle butter as well as charts with pins and strings. It’s a home only a conspiracy theorist could tolerate.

STANLEY
(muttering to himself) …it was a guinea pig, laughing, talking…but no one remembers it, no one but me…I’m not crazy, I **know** I’m not…but it doesn’t make sense…

                THE END
